    <bpmn:process id="W_W1320" name="W1320. Supplier ESG Due Diligence Assessment &amp; Sustainable Procurement Qualification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New vendor onboarding (W3.1/W224); annual vendor ESG review cycle; or trigger event (media report of vendor environmental/labor violation, DENR/DOLE action against vendor, NGO report)
Frequency: Annual assessment for top 100 vendors (by spend); triggered assessment for new vendors above PHP 5M annual spend threshold; ad-hoc for trigger events
Volume: ~100 annual assessments + ~20–30 new vendor assessments + ~5–10 trigger-event assessments per year
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Sustainability Lead, Procurement, Category Manager, VP Legal, Vendor, External ESG Auditor (for Tier 1 vendors)
Source: workflow W1320 — Supplier ESG Due Diligence Assessment &amp; Sustainable Procurement Qualification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1320_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1320_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1320_Lane2" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1320_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1320_Start4" name="New vendor onboarding (W3.1/W224); annual vendor ESG review cycle; or trigger event…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1320_Task5" name="Vendor ESG risk classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor ESG risk classification: Sustainability Lead classifies all active vendors into ESG risk tiers: (a) High ESG risk: cement/lumber/chemical manufacturers, vendors in jurisdictions with weak environmental/labor enforcement, vendors with &gt; PHP 50M annual spend, sole-source vendors for critical categories; (b) Medium ESG risk: general merchandise vendors, vendors with moderate environmental footprint, vendors in ASEAN countries with developing regulatory frameworks; (c) Low ESG risk: local Philippine vendors with verified compliance, service providers, vendors of non-hazardous goods; (d) classification drives assessment depth: High → full assessment (Step 3), Medium → self-assessment questionnaire (Step 2), Low → simplified questionnaire
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 days (annual reclassification)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1320_Task6" name="Self-Assessment Questionnaire (SAQ) distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Self-Assessment Questionnaire (SAQ) distribution: Sustainability Lead distributes ESG SAQ to Medium and Low risk vendors: (a) environmental section: energy consumption, GHG emissions, water usage, waste management, hazardous material handling, environmental certifications (ISO 14001); (b) social section: employee headcount, workplace safety record (LTIR), child labor/forced labor policy, minimum wage compliance, working hours, employee benefits; (c) governance section: anti-corruption policy, conflict of interest disclosure, data privacy compliance, regulatory violation history; (d) vendor completes SAQ via BuildRight vendor portal (W705) with supporting documentation; (e) SAQ response deadline: 30 days
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Vendor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours (distribution) + vendor response time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1320_Task7" name="Full ESG assessment for High-risk vendors">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Full ESG assessment for High-risk vendors: For High-risk vendors: (a) Sustainability Lead conducts desk review: (i) verify SAQ responses against publicly available information (company website, regulatory filings, media reports), (ii) check sanctions lists and NGO watchlists, (iii) review vendor&#x27;s own sustainability report (if available); (b) arrange on-site assessment for top 20 vendors: Sustainability Lead or External ESG Auditor visits vendor facility to inspect: (i) environmental controls (emissions, effluent, waste storage), (ii) worker conditions (safety equipment, working hours posted, fire exits), (iii) management systems (quality certifications, environmental permits, labor compliance documentation); (c) on-site assessment duration: 1–2 days per vendor; (d) assessment report prepared with findings, risk ratings, and recommended actions
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / External Auditor
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3–5 days per vendor (desk review) + 1–2 days (on-site)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1320_Task8" name="Assessment scoring &amp; vendor classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Assessment scoring &amp; vendor classification: Sustainability Lead assigns ESG score to each assessed vendor: (a) scoring criteria: Environmental (40%) + Social (30%) + Governance (30%); (b) rating scale: Green (≥ 80) — Preferred Supplier, Yellow (60–79) — Approved with Improvement Plan, Orange (40–59) — Probationary, Red (&lt; 40) — Disqualified; (c) system records ESG score with assessment date and next assessment due date; (d) ESG score visible in vendor master for Category Manager and Buyer reference in sourcing decisions
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 hour/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1320_Task9" name="Corrective action &amp; improvement plan">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Corrective action &amp; improvement plan: For Yellow and Orange-rated vendors: (a) Sustainability Lead issues Corrective Action Request (CAR) identifying specific ESG gaps and required improvements; (b) vendor submits improvement plan with timeline; (c) Sustainability Lead reviews and approves plan; (d) follow-up assessment scheduled: Yellow → 12 months, Orange → 6 months; (e) if vendor fails to improve: re-rated and potentially disqualified; (f) for Red-rated vendors: Procurement initiates vendor exit per W36 with Category Manager approval
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Vendor / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3–5 hours/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1320_Task10" name="ESG qualification in procurement decisions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: ESG qualification in procurement decisions: (a) vendor ESG score integrated into sourcing criteria per W224; (b) for tiebreaker sourcing decisions: vendor with higher ESG score preferred; (c) for government/institutional tenders (W632): ESG-qualified vendors may be required per procurement regulations; (d) Category Managers informed of vendor ESG status during assortment reviews (W1); (e) Procurement reports ESG-qualified vendor percentage in quarterly KPI dashboard
Responsible (R): Procurement / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Absorbed into existing W224/W1 processes</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1320_Task11" name="Annual reporting &amp; metrics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual reporting &amp; metrics: Sustainability Lead compiles annual supplier ESG metrics for W694 ESG report: (a) total vendors assessed vs. total active vendors; (b) ESG score distribution (Green/Yellow/Orange/Red); (c) corrective action completion rate; (d) disqualified vendors and business impact; (e) sustainable procurement spend as % of total procurement spend; (f) improvement trends year-over-year
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4–6 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1320_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1320_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1320_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1320_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-318 (ensure controlled execution — ESG Reporting &amp; Compliance (PA-25.3).) | - operational: Procurement making ESG SAQ completion a vendor portal requirement for PO processing; operational: desk review verification, on-site audits for high-risk vendors, and continuous monitoring of media/regulatory triggers; operational: developing alternative sources before disqualification per W2A and maintaining safety stock per W31
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1320_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1320_Annotation13" targetRef="W1320_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow15" sourceRef="W1320_Start4" targetRef="W1320_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow16" sourceRef="W1320_Task5" targetRef="W1320_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow17" sourceRef="W1320_Task6" targetRef="W1320_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow18" sourceRef="W1320_Task7" targetRef="W1320_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow19" sourceRef="W1320_Task8" targetRef="W1320_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow20" sourceRef="W1320_Task9" targetRef="W1320_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow21" sourceRef="W1320_Task10" targetRef="W1320_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1320_Flow22" sourceRef="W1320_Task11" targetRef="W1320_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
