    <bpmn:process id="W_W1321" name="W1321. ESG Target Setting, Quarterly Progress Tracking &amp; Board Dashboard Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual ESG strategic planning cycle (Q1); or quarterly board reporting calendar
Frequency: Annual target setting; quarterly progress review; monthly data refresh
Volume: ~15–20 ESG KPIs tracked across 5 entities, 200 stores, and 4 DCs
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Sustainability Lead, COO, CFO, CHRO, VP Legal, CEO, Board ESG Committee
Source: workflow W1321 — ESG Target Setting, Quarterly Progress Tracking &amp; Board Dashboard Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1321_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1321_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1321_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1321_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1321_Start4" name="Annual ESG strategic planning cycle (Q1); or quarterly board reporting calendar">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1321_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1321_Task5" name="Annual ESG target setting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual ESG target setting: Sustainability Lead proposes annual ESG targets for CEO and Board ESG Committee approval: (a) Environmental targets: (i) GHG emissions: reduce Scope 1+2 emissions by X% year-over-year (aligned with Philippine NDC targets), (ii) energy: reduce energy intensity (kWh/sqm) by X% per store, (iii) renewable energy: increase solar-powered stores to X of 200, (iv) water: reduce water consumption per store by X%, (v) waste diversion: increase waste diversion rate to X% (recycling + composting vs. landfill); (b) Social targets: (i) employee safety: reduce LTIR (Lost Time Injury Rate) to &lt; X per 200,000 hours worked, (ii) training: achieve minimum X training hours per employee per year, (iii) diversity: maintain or improve gender diversity ratio in management, (iv) employee engagement: achieve minimum engagement score per W629; (c) Governance targets: (i) anti-corruption training: 100% completion rate, (ii) vendor ESG assessment: cover X% of procurement spend with assessed vendors per W1320, (iii) data privacy: zero material data breaches; (d) targets set with 3-year rolling outlook; annual targets are stepping stones toward 3-year goals; (e) Board ESG Committee reviews and approves targets; targets cascaded to department heads as performance objectives
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / CEO
Accountable (A): Board ESG Committee
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1321_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1321_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1321_Task6" name="KPI baseline &amp; measurement methodology">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: KPI baseline &amp; measurement methodology: For each target: (a) Sustainability Lead documents baseline (prior year actual); (b) defines measurement methodology: data source, calculation formula, reporting frequency, responsible department; (c) configures ESG dashboard in BI system with automated data feeds where possible (energy per W692, water per W693, waste per W193, safety per W140, training per W51); (d) manual data points (e.g., vendor ESG coverage per W1320) assigned to responsible owners with quarterly submission deadlines
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1321_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1321_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1321_Task7" name="Monthly data refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly data refresh: System automatically refreshes ESG dashboard monthly: (a) energy consumption data from store/DC utility monitoring per W111; (b) GHG emissions calculated from energy data per W192 methodology; (c) water consumption from utility bills; (d) waste diversion from waste contractor reports per W502; (e) safety incidents from W140 reports; (f) training hours from HR system per W51; (g) Sustainability Lead reviews monthly data for anomalies: any KPI with &gt; 10% month-over-month variance investigated and explained
Responsible (R): System / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1321_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1321_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1321_Task8" name="Quarterly progress review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly progress review: Sustainability Lead presents quarterly ESG progress to COO and CFO: (a) each KPI: actual vs. target, year-to-date progress, trajectory (on-track/at-risk/off-track); (b) for at-risk/off-track KPIs: root cause analysis and corrective action plan with owner and deadline; (c) forward-looking projection: will the annual target be met based on current trajectory? (d) resource requests: any incremental budget needed for corrective actions (e.g., accelerated solar installation, additional safety training, waste management equipment); (e) COO approves corrective action plans and budget requests
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO / CFO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1321_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1321_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1321_Task9" name="Board ESG dashboard report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Board ESG dashboard report: Quarterly: Sustainability Lead prepares Board ESG dashboard report: (a) executive summary: overall ESG performance rating (Green/Amber/Red) across E, S, and G pillars; (b) headline KPIs with trend arrows; (c) key achievements and milestones for the quarter; (d) at-risk targets with mitigation plans; (e) regulatory update: any new or pending Philippine ESG regulations affecting BuildRight; (f) peer benchmarking: how BuildRight&#x27;s ESG performance compares to Philippine retail sector peers (if data available); (g) report presented to Board ESG Committee per W124 governance calendar
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / CEO
Accountable (A): Board ESG Committee
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1321_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1321_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1321_Task10" name="Year-end target reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Year-end target reconciliation: At annual reporting cycle (Q1): (a) Sustainability Lead reconciles actual full-year performance vs. targets for all KPIs; (b) documents explanations for any missed targets; (c) feeds results into W694 annual sustainability report; (d) proposes adjusted targets for next year based on actual performance and emerging priorities; (e) CEO incorporates ESG target achievement into department head performance evaluations per W72
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / CEO
Accountable (A): Board ESG Committee
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1321_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1321_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1321_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1321_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1321_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-318 (ensure controlled execution — ESG Reporting &amp; Compliance (PA-25.3).) | - operational: minimizing manual data points and automating feeds via ERP integration; operational: collaborative target-setting with department heads and CEO endorsement; operational: concise dashboard format (max 5 pages) and CEO championing ESG as strategic priority
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1321_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1321_Annotation12" targetRef="W1321_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
