        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1334_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W1334_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="290" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1335" name="W1335. Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) Compliance, Plastic Packaging Tracking &amp; Recovery Target Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual EPR compliance reporting deadline (per RA 11898); quarterly packaging data collection; new product introduction requiring packaging assessment
Frequency: Annual compliance report submission to DENR-EMB; quarterly packaging data tracking; monthly recovery monitoring
Volume: ~35,000 active SKUs with packaging data; estimated 5,000–8,000 tonnes of plastic packaging placed on Philippine market annually; recovery target of 20% by Year 1 increasing to 80% by Year 6 (2028) per RA 11898
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Category Manager, Procurement, Vendor, Waste Management Partner, DENR-EMB, Store Operations, Finance (EPR fee accounting)
Source: workflow W1335 — Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) Compliance, Plastic Packaging Tracking &amp; Recovery Target Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1335_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1335_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1335_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1335_Lane3" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1335_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1335_Start5" name="Annual EPR compliance reporting deadline (per RA 11898); quarterly packaging data…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1335_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1335_Task6" name="Plastic packaging inventory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Plastic packaging inventory: Sustainability Lead conducts annual packaging audit: (a) extract SKU-level packaging data from PIM per W50: packaging type (rigid plastic, flexible film, expanded polystyrene/EPS, multi-layer sachet), weight per unit, material composition, recyclability classification, (b) calculate total plastic packaging placed on market (POM): quantity sold × packaging weight per SKU, aggregated by material type, (c) identify top-20 packaging SKUs by weight — focus reduction efforts, (d) classify packaging: (i) easily recyclable (PET bottles, HDPE containers — accepted by Philippine recyclers), (ii) difficult to recycle (multi-layer sachets, EPS foam — limited recycling infrastructure in Philippines), (iii) reusable (crates, pallets — already in circular use per W328)
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 5–8 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1335_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1335_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1335_Task7" name="Recovery program management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Recovery program management: Sustainability Lead manages plastic packaging recovery: (a) partner with DENR-accredited EPR compliance schemes (e.g., Philippine Alliance for Recycling and Materials Sustainability, PARMS) for organized recovery, (b) In-store recovery: install plastic collection bins at store exits for customer return of packaging (paint cans, tile spacer bags, tool packaging), (c) Backroom recovery: collect inbound packaging (stretch film, shrink wrap, corrugated plastic) from receiving operations per W3, (d) Ecommerce packaging recovery: collect packaging from customer returns per W12 and include take-back instructions in ecommerce shipments, (e) LGU partnerships: coordinate with local government waste management programs for community collection events, (f) weigh and record recovered plastic by type and store; track recovery rate = recovered ÷ placed on market
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Store Manager / Waste Management Partner
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1335_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1335_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1335_Task8" name="Packaging reduction initiatives">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Packaging reduction initiatives: Category Manager and Procurement drive source reduction: (a) engage top-20 vendors by packaging weight to redesign packaging: reduce material, switch to recyclable mono-material, eliminate unnecessary plastic, (b) evaluate alternatives to EPS foam (used for appliance protection) — molded pulp or corrugated cardboard alternatives, (c) reduce ecommerce packaging: right-size boxes per W269, eliminate plastic void fill, use paper-based alternatives, (d) introduce reusable shopping bag program (charge PHP 5 for plastic bag per LGU ordinances in Metro Manila, Cebu), (e) track packaging reduction: weight of packaging per PHP million revenue (intensity metric)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1335_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1335_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1335_Task9" name="Quarterly recovery tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly recovery tracking: Sustainability Lead tracks recovery progress quarterly: (a) total plastic POM vs. total recovered by material type, (b) recovery rate by store, region, and material type, (c) compare to RA 11898 annual target (e.g., 40% in Year 2), (d) identify stores or material types with low recovery rates for targeted intervention, (e) if recovery rate is below target trajectory: escalate to COO with corrective action plan (e.g., add collection events, partner with additional recyclers, invest in collection infrastructure), (f) report quarterly recovery metrics to ESG dashboard per W1321
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1335_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1335_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1335_Task10" name="Annual EPR compliance report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual EPR compliance report: Sustainability Lead prepares annual EPR compliance report for DENR-EMB submission: (a) total plastic packaging POM by material type (rigid, flexible, EPS, multi-layer), (b) total plastic packaging recovered by material type, (c) recovery rate vs. statutory target, (d) description of recovery programs and initiatives, (e) packaging reduction initiatives and results, (f) planned improvements for next year, (g) supporting documentation: waste management partner certifications, LGU partnership agreements, vendor packaging redesign commitments, (h) VP Legal reviews report for regulatory completeness, (i) submit to DENR-EMB by regulatory deadline per W506 compliance calendar
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / VP Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 5–8 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1335_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1335_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1335_Task11" name="EPR fee &amp; financial accounting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: EPR fee &amp; financial accounting: Finance tracks EPR-related costs: (a) EPR compliance scheme membership fees (paid to PARMS or similar), (b) waste management partner collection and processing fees, (c) store collection bin procurement and maintenance, (d) packaging redesign investment by vendors (chargeback or cost-share per vendor agreement), (e) allocate EPR costs to sustainability expense category in GL for ESG cost reporting per W694, (f) evaluate EPR cost vs. potential non-compliance penalty (PHP 5M–20M) — compliance is cost-effective
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Absorbed into monthly closing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1335_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1335_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1335_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1335_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1335_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-318 (ensure controlled execution — ESG Reporting &amp; Compliance (PA-25.3).) | - operational: Sustainability Lead review and approval gate
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1335_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1335_Annotation13" targetRef="W1335_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
