    <bpmn:process id="W_W1396" name="W1396. Store-Level Energy Consumption Benchmarking, Carbon Footprint Estimation &amp; Reduction Target Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly utility data collection; quarterly benchmarking review; annual carbon footprint calculation
Frequency: Monthly data collection; quarterly benchmarking; annual carbon footprint estimation
Volume: 200 stores + 4 DCs × monthly utility data = ~2,448 data points/year
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Sustainability Lead, Facilities Manager, Store Manager, Finance Analyst, COO
Source: workflow W1396 — Store-Level Energy Consumption Benchmarking, Carbon Footprint Estimation &amp; Reduction Target Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1396_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1396_Lane1" name="Facilities Tech">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1396_Lane2" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1396_Lane3" name="Facilities Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1396_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1396_Start5" name="Scheduled — monthly utility data collection; quarterly benchmarking review; annual carbon…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1396_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1396_Task6" name="Monthly utility data collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly utility data collection: Facilities Technician or Store Manager enters monthly electricity (kWh) and fuel (diesel for generators, LPG for forklifts) consumption into ESG data platform — either via manual entry from utility bills or automated meter reading integration (where smart meters installed); system validates data: consumption within expected range (±30% of trailing 12-month average, adjusted for seasonal variation)
Responsible (R): Facilities Tech / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Facilities Manager
Duration: 15 min/store/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1396_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1396_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1396_Task7" name="Energy intensity benchmarking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Energy intensity benchmarking (quarterly): Sustainability Lead computes energy intensity metrics per store and DC: (a) kWh per sqm (selling area), (b) kWh per PHP revenue (energy productivity), (c) kWh per transaction; benchmark stores within peer groups: (i) Metro Manila stores vs. Metro Manila, (ii) Visayas stores vs. Visayas, (iii) Mindanao stores vs. Mindanao, (iv) DCs vs. DCs; identify top 10 energy-inefficient stores (highest kWh/sqm) and top 10 most-improved stores
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1396_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1396_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1396_Task8" name="Root cause analysis for inefficient stores">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Root cause analysis for inefficient stores: for top 10 energy-inefficient stores, Facilities Manager investigates: (a) building age and insulation quality, (b) HVAC system age and efficiency rating, (c) LED lighting retrofit status, (d) solar panel installation status (W173), (e) operating hours (24-hour stores consume more), (f) roof type and color (dark roofs absorb more heat); recommend energy efficiency improvements with ROI analysis
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1396_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1396_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1396_Task9" name="Annual carbon footprint estimation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Annual carbon footprint estimation: Sustainability Lead computes Scope 1 and Scope 2 carbon emissions: (a) Scope 1 (direct): diesel generators, LPG forklifts, company fleet vehicles — estimated ~5,000–8,000 tonnes CO2e/year; (b) Scope 2 (electricity): total kWh × Philippine grid emission factor (0.58 kg CO2e/kWh per DOE/World Bank) — estimated ~27,000–46,000 tonnes CO2e/year; (c) Total Scope 1+2: ~32,000–54,000 tonnes CO2e/year; (d) compute carbon intensity: tonnes CO2e per PHP revenue, per sqm, per transaction
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 8–16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1396_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1396_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1396_Task10" name="Reduction target tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Reduction target tracking: track progress against ESG targets (W1321): (a) energy intensity reduction target (e.g., 5% reduction in kWh/sqm over 3 years), (b) renewable energy target (e.g., solar panels on 50 stores by Year 3, per W173), (c) carbon intensity reduction target; quarterly progress report to COO and ESG Committee
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1396_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1396_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1396_Task11" name="Energy efficiency project pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Energy efficiency project pipeline: Facilities Manager maintains prioritized list of energy efficiency projects: (a) LED lighting retrofit (remaining stores without LED), (b) HVAC upgrade (inverter-type split units replacing old centralized systems), (c) smart building controls (motion-sensor lighting in low-traffic areas, programmable thermostats), (d) solar panel installation per W173, (e) generator replacement with more fuel-efficient models; each project includes estimated energy savings (kWh/year), carbon reduction (tonnes CO2e/year), capital cost, and payback period
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1396_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1396_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1396_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1396_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1396_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-318 (ensure controlled execution — ESG Reporting &amp; Compliance (PA-25.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1396_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1396_Annotation13" targetRef="W1396_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1396_Flow15" sourceRef="W1396_Start5" targetRef="W1396_Task6" />
