    <bpmn:process id="W_W1397" name="W1397. Philippine SEC Sustainability Reporting (Memo Circular No. 4) Annual Data Collection &amp; Report Preparation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — annual; SEC reporting deadline (typically within 120 days from fiscal year-end, aligned with Annual Report submission)
Frequency: Annual
Volume: 1 comprehensive sustainability report per year for BuildRight Holdings Inc. (privately held; prepared voluntarily); covers all 5 subsidiaries
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Sustainability Lead, CFO, Controller, CHRO, COO, VP Supply Chain, Legal, Corporate Secretary, External Sustainability Auditor (if engaged)
Source: workflow W1397 — Philippine SEC Sustainability Reporting (Memo Circular No. 4) Annual Data Collection &amp; Report Preparation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1397_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1397_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1397_Lane2" name="Data Stewards">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1397_Lane3" name="Reviewers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1397_Lane4" name="Audit &amp; Risk Committee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1397_Lane5" name="Corporate Secretary">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1397_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1397_Start7" name="Scheduled — annual; SEC reporting deadline (typically within 120 days from fiscal…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task8" name="Reporting calendar and responsibility matrix">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Reporting calendar and responsibility matrix (Q4, 2 months before fiscal year-end): Sustainability Lead publishes annual reporting calendar with data collection deadlines for each function: (a) Finance (Controller): economic performance data — revenue, taxes paid, community investments, capital expenditure by region; (b) Operations (COO): environmental data — energy consumption, carbon emissions (W1396), water consumption, waste generated and diverted, packaging materials (W1335 EPR compliance); (c) Supply Chain (VP Supply Chain): responsible sourcing data — vendor ESG assessments (W1320), local procurement spend, conflict mineral sourcing (if applicable); (d) HR (CHRO): social data — workforce diversity, employee turnover, training hours, health and safety incidents (W695, W24.1), labor relations, community engagement; (e) Governance (Corporate Secretary): board diversity, anti-corruption training, whistleblower reports, ethics policy compliance
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task9" name="Data collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Data collection (Q1, first 8 weeks after fiscal year-end): each function submits data per responsibility matrix: (a) Sustainability Lead provides standardized data collection templates (Excel or online form) with definitions, units, and prior-year comparatives; (b) each function&#x27;s data steward completes templates; (c) Sustainability Lead validates data completeness and consistency — cross-check against internal sources (GL for financial data, HRIS for HR data, utility bills for environmental data)
Responsible (R): Data Stewards / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): Function Heads
Duration: 4–8 hours/function</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task10" name="Materiality assessment refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Materiality assessment refresh (every 2 years): Sustainability Lead conducts materiality assessment to identify the most significant ESG topics for BuildRight&#x27;s stakeholders: (a) survey key stakeholders (investors, employees, customers, suppliers, LGU partners); (b) map ESG topics by stakeholder importance vs. business impact; (c) update materiality matrix; (d) ensure report covers all material topics per GRI requirements
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 20–30 hours (biennial)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task11" name="Report drafting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Report drafting (Q1, weeks 8–12): Sustainability Lead drafts sustainability report per SEC MC No. 4 format: (a) Economic section: financial performance highlights, economic value generated and distributed, indirect economic impacts (employment in provincial communities, tax payments to LGUs), procurement spend with local suppliers; (b) Environmental section: energy consumption and intensity (W1396), GHG emissions Scope 1+2 (W1396, W1334), water consumption, waste management, packaging (W1335), environmental compliance incidents (W801); (c) Social section: employment statistics, diversity and inclusion, training and development, occupational health and safety (W695, W24.1), community engagement (W1106), customer safety and satisfaction; (d) Governance section: board composition and diversity, anti-corruption, ethics, data privacy (W1203), supply chain responsibility
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 40–60 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task12" name="Internal review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Internal review: CFO, Legal, and COO review draft report: (a) CFO verifies financial data accuracy and alignment with audited financial statements; (b) Legal reviews for regulatory compliance, forward-looking statement risk, and legal privilege considerations; (c) COO validates operational data accuracy; (d) Sustainability Lead incorporates feedback and finalizes draft
Responsible (R): Reviewers / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8–16 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task13" name="Board/Audit &amp; Risk Committee review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Board/Audit &amp; Risk Committee review: Sustainability Lead presents final draft to Audit &amp; Risk Committee for approval; committee reviews: (a) alignment with BuildRight&#x27;s stated ESG strategy, (b) consistency with financial reporting, (c) adequacy of disclosures, (d) approval for external publication
Responsible (R): Audit &amp; Risk Committee
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task14" name="External assurance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: External assurance (if required or voluntary): if BuildRight engages an external sustainability auditor (recommended for credibility but not yet mandated by SEC), Sustainability Lead coordinates: (a) provide auditor with data source documentation and evidence; (b) management representation letter; (c) auditor issues limited or reasonable assurance opinion
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / External Auditor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8–16 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1397_Task15" name="SEC submission and publication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: SEC submission and publication: Corporate Secretary submits sustainability report as part of Annual Report (SEC Form 17-A) to SEC within 120 days of fiscal year-end; Sustainability Lead publishes report on BuildRight website and sustainability microsite; notify investors and stakeholders via corporate communications
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1397_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1397_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1397_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1397_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-318 (ensure controlled execution — ESG Reporting &amp; Compliance (PA-25.3).) | - operational: Sustainability Lead review and approval gate
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
