    <bpmn:process id="W_W5578" name="W5578. Environmental Data Capture, Emission-Factor Governance &amp; GHG Transaction Batch Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly environmental-data close; a Payables utility/fuel invoice posting; an Inventory issue of a tracked consumable; an emission-factor publication (DOE grid factor, IPCC revision); a new site, asset or fuel source entering the estate
Frequency: Continuous automatic capture from the source subledgers; monthly batch close; annual emission-factor and hierarchy review
Volume: 205 sites (200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ) × ~4 tracked sources each ≈ ~820 usage streams; ~2,500 environmental transactions/month from Payables, Inventory and Assets, plus manual batches for sources with no subledger document
Owner: Sustainability Lead
Participants: Sustainability Lead, Facilities Manager (site energy and water), Fleet Manager (fuel — links to VS-192), Finance Controller (the subledger documents the capture rides), AP Supervisor (links to VS-15.1), Data Scientist (factor modelling), IT Application Manager (links to W132), External Carbon Verification Auditor
Source: workflow W5578 — Environmental Data Capture, Emission-Factor Governance &amp; GHG Transaction Batch Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5578_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5578_Lane1" name="Sustainability Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5578_Lane2" name="Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5578_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5578_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5578_Start5" name="Monthly environmental-data close; a Payables utility/fuel invoice posting; an Inventory…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5578_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5578_Task6" name="Sustainability Lead maintain the environmental reference data in the suite…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sustainability Lead maintain the environmental reference data in the suite: emission types and their gases, sources and source usage definitions per site and asset class, the unit-of-measure classification and conversions the quantities are normalized through, and the organization hierarchy the roll-up follows; a new site, fuel or refrigerant does not begin reporting until its source and UOM conversion exist
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 4–8 hours/change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5578_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5578_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5578_Task7" name="Sustainability Lead and Data Scientist govern the emission factors: the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sustainability Lead and Data Scientist govern the emission factors: the Philippine grid factor for purchased electricity, mobile and stationary combustion factors, refrigerant global-warming potentials and the Scope 3 spend factors; each factor carries its published source, effective-from date and the cycle it first applied to, and a superseded factor is never edited in place — it is end-dated so prior periods keep restating to the same number
Responsible (R): Data Scientist / Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): Sustainability Lead
Duration: 8–16 hours/annual review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5578_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5578_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5578_Task8" name="The suite captures usage automatically as the source documents post: utility…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: The suite captures usage automatically as the source documents post: utility, fuel and waste-disposal invoices at Payables entry and match (links to VS-15.1), tracked-consumable issues at the Inventory miscellaneous transaction, asset-linked sources from the asset register (links to W39), and site sources from the lease and property records (links to VS-42); the capture carries the quantity and its UOM, not an estimate
Responsible (R): System / AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5578_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5578_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5578_Task9" name="Sustainability Lead enter transaction batches by hand for the sources that…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Sustainability Lead enter transaction batches by hand for the sources that carry no subledger document — self-generated solar output (links to W173), tenant-submetered concession consumption, third-party logistics fuel reported by the carrier, and water drawn under a shared-facility arrangement; every manual batch names its evidence document so the assurance sample can trace it
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead / Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): Sustainability Lead
Duration: 6–10 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5578_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5578_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5578_Task10" name="Sustainability Lead close the month: reconcile captured quantities to the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Sustainability Lead close the month: reconcile captured quantities to the source subledgers and to the utility and fleet records the reporting workflows also read (W111, W692, W327), investigate sites whose consumption moves more than the variance threshold, and release the period so the emissions figures behind W1334, W3466, W5481 and W1396 are drawn from one closed ledger rather than five parallel extracts
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 8–12 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5578_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5578_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5578_Task11" name="Sustainability Lead prepare the assurance extract for the annual external…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Sustainability Lead prepare the assurance extract for the annual external verification (links to W1334): the transaction-level ledger with its factors, the factor change history with effective dates, the manual-batch evidence index, and the restatement record for any period reopened after a factor correction
Responsible (R): Sustainability Lead
Accountable (A): Sustainability Lead
Duration: 16–24 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5578_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5578_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5578_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5578_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5578_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-318 (ensure controlled execution — ESG Reporting &amp; Compliance (PA-25.3).) | - operational: no emission factor is edited in place — superseded factors are end-dated so prior periods restate identically | - operational: every manually entered transaction batch names the evidence document that supports it | - operational: the period is closed and reconciled before any reporting workflow draws its figures from it
Owner: Sustainability Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5578_Assoc14" sourceRef="W5578_Annotation13" targetRef="W5578_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
